# This repository's first shell script arrived with scripts/renovate-local.sh,
# and it is run by bash - from WSL on a Windows box, and inside the Linux CI
# image if a lane ever calls it. Without this rule core.autocrlf=true hands a
# Windows clone CRLF and bash dies on the trailing carriage return with errors
# that name the wrong culprit: "set: pipefail\r: invalid option name",
# "$'\r': command not found". OxidANT carries the same rule for the same reason,
# with a note that it is exactly how a local container build once failed.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
